## 6. Technical Walkthrough

### 6.1 Reconnaissance

```bash
echo '<TARGET_IP> 2million.htb' | sudo tee -a /etc/hosts
nmap -sC -sV -Pn -oN scans/nmap_initial.txt <TARGET_IP>
```

| Port | Service | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| 22/tcp | OpenSSH | Password authentication enabled |
| 80/tcp | nginx | Redirects to `http://2million.htb` |

The web application is a replica of the legacy Hack The Box platform. `Join → Join HTB` leads
to `/invite`.

### 6.2 Invite Code Bypass → Authenticated Session

1. View page source → `<script defer src="/js/inviteapi.min.js">`.
2. Deobfuscate the packer (`de4js`, or replace `eval` with `console.log` in the browser console).
3. Discovered functions: `verifyInviteCode()` and **`makeInviteCode()`**.
4. `POST /api/v1/invite/how/to/generate` → ROT13 hint → `POST /api/v1/invite/generate` → Base64
   invite code.
5. Submit the code on `/invite`, register on `/register`, log in on `/login`.

> **Methodology note:** every client-side asset is attacker-controlled input. Obfuscation is
> not a security boundary.

### 6.3 API Enumeration

```bash
export SESS='PHPSESSID=<SESSION_COOKIE>'

curl -i http://2million.htb/api                      # 401 without a session
curl -s http://2million.htb/api/v1 --cookie "$SESS" | jq   # full endpoint catalogue
```

Interesting routes: `GET /admin/auth`, `POST /admin/vpn/generate`, `PUT /admin/settings/update`.

### 6.4 Privilege Escalation to Administrator

See **HTB-2M-02**. The decisive observation was that the endpoint returned
`Invalid content type.` **instead of `401`** — proof that the authorisation gate had already
been passed. Each subsequent error message was used to build a valid request incrementally.

### 6.5 Command Injection → Foothold

See **HTB-2M-03**. Shell stabilisation:

```bash
python3 -c 'import pty;pty.spawn("/bin/bash")'
export TERM=xterm
# CTRL+Z
stty raw -echo; fg
reset
```

### 6.6 Lateral Movement

See **HTB-2M-04**. `.env` → `admin:SuperDuperPass123` → SSH → 🚩 `user.txt`.

### 6.7 Privilege Escalation to root

See **HTB-2M-05**. Kernel enumeration → CVE-2023-0386 → 🚩 `root.txt`.

### 6.8 Post-Exploitation (bonus)

`/root/thank_you.json` contains a layered-encoded message from the HTB team. Decoding chain:

```
URL decode → HEX decode → Base64 decode → XOR (key: "HackTheBox", UTF-8)
```

Decoded with [CyberChef](https://gchq.github.io/CyberChef/). A neat exercise in recognising
encoding layers by their characteristic alphabets and structural markers.

